# Forge KS visual catalog governance

When changing any visual page, layout, section, component, primitive, style, diagram, interaction, or desktop/app interface:

1. Identify the affected visual hash or explain why no visual hash applies.
2. Check `docs/design/catalog/visual-registry.yaml`.
3. Check the matching design contract under `docs/design/catalog/**/{HASH}-*.md` or family contract for `contract_status: family-covered`.
4. Preserve the existing hash for compatible copy, accessibility, bug-fix, and token refinements.
5. Allocate a new hash for a breaking visual role/anatomy change or a new reusable visual object (`node tools/design-catalog/allocate-visual-hash.mjs`).
6. Ensure visual roots emit both `hash="XYZ"` and `data-ks-hash="XYZ"` (Python `ks_hash_attrs`, React `ksVisualAttrs` / `ksReactPrimitiveAttrs`).
7. Update screenshot status or expected screenshot references when the expected look changes.
8. Run `python3 generator/build-showcase.py` and `node tools/design-catalog/check-visual-catalog.mjs --repo . --registry docs/design/catalog/visual-registry.yaml --showcase showcase`.
9. After adding sources, run `node tools/design-catalog/inventory-ks-visuals.mjs`; add new `docs/design/*.md` paths (outside `docs/design/catalog/`) to **Kdt** `source_paths` when `check-visual-catalog` warns.

Do not treat design catalog updates as optional when visual behavior or expected appearance changes.
